Focus on key economic releases scheduled for the rest of the week (GDP, jobs data, inflation figures, etc.). Model different scenarios (positive vs. negative surprises) and their potential impact on the S&P 500. Weigh the potential upside against the downside risk. If the market reaction to previous similar data was significant, amplify your conviction score. Adjust sentiment based on your predicted scenario and factor in the remaining trading days. A high impact data release on Friday, where consensus has shifted multiple times, warrants both sentiment and conviction close to 0 until 10 minutes after the release.